## 3. Knowledge Graph Automation & Sync
*   Use the local `.code-review-graph/graph.db` to identify downstream calls and component bounds before starting architectural edits.
*   Always synchronize the graph after modifying files or adding classes using:
    ```bash
    graphify build
    ```

---

## 4. Subagent Delegation Rule
*   Break down larger implementations using modular checklist items.
*   Ephemereal subagents must be supplied only with a focused context (relevant classes, specific requirements in `spec.md`, and the graph relations) to prevent token bloat and context drift.
*   All code written by subagents must undergo compilation check (`./mvnw clean compile`) and unit test verification (`./mvnw test`).
